regular medication.","bbox":{"x0":0.08601456337538488,"y0":0.3227864195014158,"x1":0.47243410640507727,"y1":0.33751108509692446},"ocr":true},{"page":1,"seq":10,"kind":"section_header","text":"Findings and treatment","bbox":{"x0":0.08608492912333761,"y0":0.35474471048504064,"x1":0.2842689545294386,"y1":0.36831912575139586},"ocr":true},{"page":1,"seq":11,"kind":"text","text":"The patient presented with acute onset of diarhea and vomiting. Examination revealed mild dehydration and tenderness in the epigastrium. Stool examination was negative for parasites and bacterial pathogens. Viral antigen testing was not performed. Treatment included oral rehydration solution, ondansetron for nausea, and symptomatic care. The patient was advised to maintain hydration and return if symptoms worsen or persist beyond 72 hours.","bbox":{"x0":0.08470442735112485,"y0":0.3861185468173745,"x1":0.9066762111959,"y1":0.4492905873317157},"ocr":true},{"page":1,"seq":12,"kind":"text","text":"Attending physician: Alexandra Nagy Signature and stamp","bbox":{"x0":0.08467632175067505,"y0":0.491340180851103,"x1":0.3083830250972356,"y1":0.5042101247958641},"ocr":true}],"parser":"docling","seconds":0.68}